      "text": "one jot or one tittle shall in no wise pass, Matt. 5:18 (3 Ne. 12:18). Heaven and earth shall pass away, Matt. 24:35 (Mark 13:31; Luke 21:33; 2 Pet. 3:10; 3 Ne. 26:3; D&C 29:23; JS—M 1:35). let this cup pass from me, Matt. 26:39 (Mark 14:35). he passing through the midst of them, Luke 4:30. a certain priest … passed by on the other side, Luke 10:31. easier for heaven and earth to pass, Luke 16:17. is passed from death unto life, John 5:24. fashion of this world passeth away, 1 Cor. 7:31. old things are passed away, 2 Cor. 5:17 (D&C 29:24; 63:49). love of Christ, which passeth knowledge, Eph. 3:19. we have a great high priest, that is passed into the heavens, Heb. 4:14. the world passeth away, 1 Jn. 2:17. we have passed from death unto life, 1 Jn. 3:14. first heaven and the first earth were passed away, Rev. 21:1. former things are passed away, Rev. 21:4.",
